{ Choose the course move. Explain its purpose and one resource for White. Other moves may also be sound. Answer: f5. Challenges e4 after the f6 square has been cleared. The center and White's king placement must justify the break. Close the center, reroute the knight, then choose the pawn break. White's broader aim: White develops behind a space advantage. Re1, Be3 and exchanges on e5 can stop Black from getting a routine kingside race. }
10... f5 *

