{ Choose the course move. Explain its purpose and one resource for White. Other moves may also be sound. Answer: Ng6. Brings a knight toward kingside entry squares while maintaining central influence. The pawn wave creates entry squares for pieces. White's broader aim: White normally expands with c5, opens c-files, and uses the e1 knight to support the queenside or defend. White can also challenge your attack with g4. }
13... Ng6 *

