{ Which knight must move before ...f5, and what is White's fastest central or queenside reply? Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: White's d5/e4 chain faces Black's d6/e5 chain. Neither d-pawn can move straight forward. The chain gives a direction to the plans, but either side can open it with a pawn lever. Prepare ...f5 by moving the f6 knight and coordinating the pieces. If ...f4 fixes the center, use the gained space to bring pieces toward the king. White: White expands with c5 and may invade on the c-file. White can also undermine the attack with g4. Count how many moves your pieces need. }
*

