[SetUp "1"]

{ Name the first piece that should join the attack and the line it will use. Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: The f4 pawn gains space and restricts White's pieces. It also fixes targets and closes lines your own rooks might otherwise use. Support the pawn with ...g5 only if the pieces can join. Typical jobs include ...Ng6, ...Nf6, ...h5 and queen access. Identify the entry square, not just the next pawn. White: White may play c5, g4, or bring defenders to f2 and d3. If the attack slows, the queenside weaknesses can become decisive. }
*

