[SetUp "1"]

{ Which captures can change the center immediately, and what file opens after each? Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: White's c5 attacks d6 while Black's f5 attacks e4. The locked center can open from either end, so a one-wing evaluation is incomplete. Compare ...f4, ...fxe4 and a d-pawn exchange only after analyzing White's captures. Preserve piece activity if the pawn skeleton changes. White: White can trade on d6 or f5 and use open files before Black finishes regrouping. }
*

