{ What would change your decision between ...b5 and ...e5? Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: Black has ...Nc6, ...a6 and ...Rb8. White's f3 pawn supports the center but delays natural king-knight development. Prepare ...b5 when the captures work. If White restrains it with a4, compare ...e5. If White closes with d5, answer the knight attack first. White: Bh6, h4 and g4 can threaten the king. White may avoid long castling and turn the queenside opening into a central game. }
