[SetUp "1"]

{ Which white piece supports e5, and why is exchanging it potentially useful? Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: White has a d5 wedge and an e4/f4 center; Black has d6 and c5. Black's e-pawn has been exchanged, opening the e-file. Pressure e4, challenge the knight that supports e5, and develop rapidly. Prepare queenside expansion only when d6 and the king are secure. White: White threatens e5 with tempo or a kingside attack. A passive setup lets the space advantage grow. }
