{ What preparation would make ...d5 a freeing break rather than a pawn sacrifice? Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: White's d-pawn has disappeared. Pawns on c4 and e4 control d5, restricting Black's central break. Develop toward a supported ...d5 or create useful queenside pressure. Trade a pair of pieces when it reduces the cramp without conceding a permanent weakness. White: White can maintain the bind, improve pieces and attack d6. An unsupported ...d5 may simply lose a pawn. }
