{ Which central exchange activates the g2 bishop, and what must Black recheck afterward? Explain Black's plan after any necessary White reply. Answer: Both kings have fianchettoed bishops. White's g2 bishop adds a defender and a long-range attacker, changing the value of a kingside pawn advance. Develop central pressure with ...Re8, ...exd4 and a knight on c5 when justified. ...c6 can support a later ...d5 break. White: White may open the long diagonal with a central exchange. An exposed b7 pawn or loose c6 piece can then become a target. }
